  "title": "Apply Loyalty Discount to Active Subscribers",
  "prompt": "A subscription-box retailer wants to reward long-term customers. The `subscriber_boxes` table tracks each customer's monthly box with `customer_id`, `box_month` (DATE), `base_price` (DECIMAL(10,2)), and `final_price` (DECIMAL(10,2)). Management has decided to apply a 15% discount to boxes for customers who have been subscribed for at least 6 months as of their box_month. Write a single UPDATE statement that reduces `final_price` by 15% for any row where the customer's earliest box_month (across all their rows) is at least 6 months before that row's box_month. After the UPDATE, write a SELECT statement that returns all columns from `subscriber_boxes` ordered by `customer_id`, `box_month` to confirm the changes.",
